    <% include ./partials/navbar.ejs %>

      <main>
          <p class="animated fadeIn page-title">Skills</p>

          <section class="section animated fadeIn">
            <div class="container">
              <p class="section-sub">The tools and methods I use to take retail data problems from question to production.</p>

              <div class="feature-grid">

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:code"></span>
                  <h4>Programming Languages</h4>
                  <p>Python for data science and production machine learning, SQL for everything data, plus R for statistics and JavaScript / Node.js for building data apps.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">Python</span><span class="chip">SQL</span><span class="chip">R</span><span class="chip">JavaScript</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:chart-histogram"></span>
                  <h4>Data Analysis &amp; Statistics</h4>
                  <p>Cleaning, reshaping, and feature engineering with Pandas and NumPy, plus the exploratory analysis, statistical modeling, and hypothesis testing that keep conclusions honest.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">Pandas</span><span class="chip">NumPy</span><span class="chip">SciPy</span><span class="chip">statsmodels</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:machine-learning-model"></span>
                  <h4>Machine Learning &amp; AI</h4>
                  <p>Classification, regression, recommendation, and forecasting with scikit-learn, XGBoost, and TensorFlow, plus LLM-powered and agentic AI workflows.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">scikit-learn</span><span class="chip">XGBoost</span><span class="chip">TensorFlow</span><span class="chip">LLMs</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:chart-line-data"></span>
                  <h4>Forecasting &amp; Optimization</h4>
                  <p>Time-series and machine learning forecasters, from ARIMA to gradient boosting, turned into demand plans, inventory targets, and allocation decisions.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">ARIMA</span><span class="chip">Prophet</span><span class="chip">Gradient Boosting</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:chart-multitype"></span>
                  <h4>Data Visualization &amp; Apps</h4>
                  <p>Seaborn, Matplotlib, and Plotly for analysis, Folium and GeoPandas for maps, and award-winning Streamlit apps so stakeholders can explore the work themselves.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">Plotly</span><span class="chip">Seaborn</span><span class="chip">Streamlit</span><span class="chip">Folium</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:cloud"></span>
                  <h4>Cloud &amp; MLOps</h4>
                  <p>Building and deploying pipelines on GCP and AWS, with Databricks and Spark for scale and Kubeflow plus CI/CD to keep them reproducible and monitored.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">GCP</span><span class="chip">AWS</span><span class="chip">Databricks</span><span class="chip">Kubeflow</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:data-base"></span>
                  <h4>Databases</h4>
                  <p>SQL across MySQL, PostgreSQL, and BigQuery for analytical and production workloads, and MongoDB for document data.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">MySQL</span><span class="chip">PostgreSQL</span><span class="chip">BigQuery</span><span class="chip">MongoDB</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                  <span class="iconify" data-icon="carbon:branch"></span>
                  <h4>Version Control &amp; Collaboration</h4>
                  <p>Git and GitHub day to day for branching, code review, and shipping readable, well-documented code a team can maintain. I also teach these practices at the University of Denver.</p>
                  <div class="chips">
                    <span class="chip">Git</span><span class="chip">GitHub</span><span class="chip">CI/CD</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

